course: dictionary
lesson: 2969
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The word drum can be a thing you play, a big container, or an action. To find the right meaning, read the words around it. These are its context, and they leave clues.
explain: «A boy in New York practised the drums for hours every day» tells you a drum is a musical instrument, because you practise an instrument. «Old oil drums» in another sentence means large containers, because oil is a liquid that is stored in something.
explain: «On a park lawn a gull may stamp its feet up and down» and «the drumming feels like rain to the worms» show that drumming here is a verb. It means tapping again and again, not playing music. Try your meaning in the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Drum can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). Drums, drumming and drummed are all forms of the same word.
fact: As a noun, a drum is a musical instrument with a hollow body and skin stretched over it, played by hitting it.
fact: As a noun, a drum can also be a large container shaped like a cylinder, for liquids, such as an oil drum.
fact: To drum means to play a drum, or to tap again and again, as in «drum your fingers».
fact: The eardrum is the thin skin inside your ear. It vibrates when sound reaches it.
exercise: In «A boy in New York practised the drums for hours every day», what are the drums? | A way of teaching by repeating | Containers for oil | *A musical instrument you hit to make a sound | The thin skin inside your ear
exercise: «The drumming feels like rain to the worms.» What does drumming mean here? | Storing oil in a large container | Playing a tune on a drum kit | Hearing a sound through the ear | *Tapping again and again
exercise: Which part of the ear vibrates when sound reaches it? | *The eardrum | The gorilla's chest | Oil drum | The drum kit
test: «Old oil drums» are used in the sentence about instruments made from what was at hand. What is an oil drum? | *A large container for liquids such as oil | A tap on a bowl | The skin inside your ear | A drum you play with sticks
test: A teacher wants pupils to drum multiplication tables into their heads. What does drum into mean? | *To teach them by repeating them many times | To store them in an oil drum | To make a loud noise in class | To play them on a drum kit
exam: A child reads a sentence with drum in it and is unsure which meaning fits. What should they do first? | *Read the words around it for clues and try the meaning in the sentence | Always pick the first meaning in the dictionary | Count the letters in drum | Guess and never check
